From e45d4efa2159e96d7967a4ccab951f04ece4a17e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@debian.lab.local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:30:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] ASoC: ice1712: PHASE 88 has no consumer AC'97 codec

The CODEC byte (offset 06) of the PHASE 88 EEPROM is 0x0f: four ADCs and
four DACs, and bit 4 clear, which tells the driver that a consumer AC'97
codec is present.  It is not.  The AC-Link does not answer at all - even
after a cold reset every register reads back as 0xffff - so the probe
first waits through the AC'97 reset timeouts and then reports:

  Consumer PCM code does not work well at the moment --jk
  AC'97 0 does not respond - RESET
  AC'97 0 access is not valid [0xffffffff], removing mixer.
  cannot initialize ac97 for consumer, skipped

and still creates the consumer and consumer (DS) PCM devices, which have
no codec behind them: opening them fails (or used to oops, see the
previous patch) and the sample rate rules cannot be derived.

All converters of this board are the four AK4524 on the multi-track I2S
interface, selected by ACLink = 0x80 (ICE1712_CFG_PRO_I2S), and the
Terratec Windows driver does not touch the AC-Link of a PHASE 88 either.
Set ICE1712_CFG_NO_CON_AC97 in the CODEC byte before it is written to PCI
configuration 0x60, the same way the DMX 6Fire (which also has all its
converters on the multi-track interface and no consumer codec) is handled
just above.  The consumer AC-Link then stays in reset, the consumer IRQs
stay masked and only the 10 out / 12 in "ICE1712 multi" device is created,
matching the hardware and the Windows driver.
---
 sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c b/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
index c276f7068..18e4f43a4 100644
--- a/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
+++ b/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
@@ -2293,12 +2293,26 @@ static int snd_ice1712_chip_init(struct snd_ice1712 *ice)
 	outb(ICE1712_NATIVE, ICEREG(ice, CONTROL));
 	udelay(200);
 	if (ice->eeprom.subvendor == ICE1712_SUBDEVICE_DMX6FIRE &&
-	    !ice->dxr_enable)
+	    !ice->dxr_enable) {
 		/*  Set eeprom value to limit active ADCs and DACs to 6;
 		 *  Also disable AC97 as no hardware in standard 6fire card/box
 		 *  Note: DXR extensions are not currently supported
 		 */
 		ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC] = 0x3a;
+	} else if (ice->eeprom.subvendor == ICE1712_SUBDEVICE_PHASE88) {
+		/*
+		 * The EEPROM of the PHASE 88 advertises a consumer AC'97
+		 * codec, but the board does not carry one - the AC'97 link
+		 * does not answer even after a cold reset (every register
+		 * reads back as 0xffff).  All converters of this card are the
+		 * AKM codecs on the multitrack I2S interface, and the original
+		 * Terratec driver does not touch the AC'97 link either.
+		 * Without this quirk the probe wastes two seconds in the
+		 * AC'97 reset and creates consumer PCM devices that have no
+		 * codec behind them.
+		 */
+		ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC] |= ICE1712_CFG_NO_CON_AC97;
+	}
 	pci_write_config_byte(ice->pci, 0x60, ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC]);
 	pci_write_config_byte(ice->pci, 0x61, ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_ACLINK]);
 	pci_write_config_byte(ice->pci, 0x62, ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_I2SID]);
